      "why": "iterative is the lowest-power family (single datapath, no per-stage registers, no k-way parallelism). It is the only family that can plausibly minimise power_index while still meeting 50 MSPS, since its throughput is Fmax/(N+3). To hit 50 MSPS it needs a high Fmax, which argues for keeping N modest (10..20) and the datapath narrow (W 14..20). The accuracy constraint (<=2^-12) is met by W>=14 with N>=10 and round; the W/N/guard trade-off is exactly the power-vs-accuracy curve the spec wants mapped, so I focus the budget here."
