      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "unrolled_k raises throughput to Fmax/(ceil(N/k)+3) at the cost of k-way parallel datapath area and power. It is the second-cheapest family and gives a different point on the power-vs-accuracy/throughput curve: for the same accuracy (same W/N/guard) it trades extra power for higher Fmax margin, which can let it meet 50 MSPS at a lower clock (lower power_index) than iterative, or vice-versa. k is capped at 4 because beyond that the parallel area/power grows faster than the latency benefit, so the interesting trade-off lives at k=2..4. Same W/N/guard ranges as iterative so the two fronts are directly comparable on accuracy."
    }
