  "rationale": "The spec minimises power_index subject to throughput>=50 MSPS and max_abs_err<=2^-12, with accuracy as the trade-off. Of the families I may use, iterative is the power floor (shared datapath, no parallelism, no per-stage registers) and unrolled_k is the next-cheapest (k-way parallelism, shared FSM). Both can plausibly meet 50 MSPS: iterative via a high Fmax with modest N, unrolled_k via k>1 shortening the result period. I therefore split the budget evenly between them so the merged front covers the full power-vs-accuracy trade-off rather than a single corner. Ranges are narrowed to where the constraints bind: W 14..20 (W<14 cannot reach 2^-12 accuracy; W>20 adds area/power with no accuracy benefit once N is sufficient), N 10..20 (N<10 risks missing 2^-12; N>20 lowers Fmax and raises latency with no accuracy gain), angle_guard -1..2 and frac_guard 0..2 (small guards keep the datapath narrow for power while still giving the accuracy headroom), and rounding over both choices since round typically buys accuracy at a small power cost. k is limited to 2..4 for unrolled_k to stay in the region where parallelism helps throughput without dominating power. This focuses the 100-eval budget on the feasible, constraint-relevant part of the space so the hypervolume is spent mapping the actual trade-off curve."
}

